The first implementation is now in place. It stays in the paper’s native group-sequence language, uses the paper’s \(k=\exp(G)\) rank-two regime, and plants a balanced zero-sum subset with no one- or two-term shortcut. I’m now stress-testing the centered LLL embedding and exact meet-in-the-middle baseline; these are the decisive checks for whether the construction is genuinely usable.
